  "2026-10-21T16:18:24.839Z",codex-agent,"PR #5 review round: verified unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u2YPE. Capture consolidation corpus and lexical proposals under the writer lock, release before loopback embedding HTTP requests, preserve advisory output and lexical apply semantics. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Self-review also found semantic recall holds the same lock during embedding; fix that instance while preserving atomic emitted-only counters and retrying changed corpus snapshots. Add slow-loopback concurrency regressions and function-only revert proofs; run unchanged npm and Bun release gates with isolated Git identity."
  "2026-10-21T16:22:51.966Z",codex-agent,"Implemented review thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u2YPE and same-class recall correction. Slow loopback fixture withholds both embedding batches for a 17-memory preview while separate writer processes complete; lexical proposals and captured corpus remain stable and durable bytes change only from those writers. Recall releases the lock for document and query embeddings, retries insertions and content revisions, and atomically increments current counters without retrying counter-only drift. Typecheck, lint and zero-duplication checks passed. Function-only consolidate revert fails its targeted regression (0 passed, 1 failed, exit 1: writer blocked while embedding response is withheld); restored implementation passes (1 passed, 0 failed). Function-only recall revert fails with the same contention assertion (0 passed, 1 failed, exit 1). Final restored recall proof and full unchanged-threshold release gates follow."
  "2026-10-21T16:23:15.495Z",codex-agent,"Completed both behavioural revert proofs against PR head 57e4a58: replace only consolidate with its original function and node --test --test-name-pattern=\"semantic preview releases\" test/semantic.test.ts fails 0/1 with the withheld-response writer assertion; restoration passes 1/1. Replace only recall and node --test --test-name-pattern=\"semantic recall releases\" test/semantic.test.ts likewise fails 0/1; restoration passes 1/1, including insertion/edit retries and counter-only concurrency during a blocked query embedding. Tests execute TypeScript sources directly. All functions are restored; no thresholds or dependency pins changed. Full release checks are next."
