  "2026-10-21T16:39:54.772Z",codex-agent,"Verified source commit d1f105cc1c95a5b4c881a151a7f8d0a33c19f94b in CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/actions/runs/39635936425: Node 22 and Node 26 passed every npm release-check component, each with 186/186 suite tests and 2/2 packed npm/Bun consumers. Node 26 also ran bun run release:check successfully with 186/186 suite tests and 2/2 consumers. Each measured 22 intended source files at 100/100/100/100, zero duplication and zero production vulnerabilities; all 96 declarations documented. The existing local JWT privacy wall-clock failure passed its immediate focused retry and all CI executions. A redundant local full npm retry was stopped after complete source-head CI success; it is not claimed as a passing local gate. No test, timing limit, coverage threshold, dependency pin, lock policy or tracked build-output policy was weakened. Review inventory refreshed: exactly one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6u2YPE; no outside-diff findings in the latest CodeRabbit review. Whole-diff review fixed the recall instance too and corrected stale architecture text. No thread replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was established. Open limits: continuously changing corpus content can delay recall retries; the existing development-only glob advisory remains tracked in pm-memory-eafx. Leave the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
