  "2026-10-22T11:17:33.476Z",codex-agent,"Both independent behavioural reverts reject the new regressions: restoring only the old remember content-equality condition makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^review pin-only\" test/semantic.test.ts fail 0 passed/1 failed (pin changes the stored content timestamp). Restoring only memoryVectors from the pre-fix head makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^review rejection markers\" test/semantic.test.ts fail 0 passed/1 failed (no rejection marker is persisted). Each source was restored immediately afterward. Before reverts the four targeted regressions passed 4/4, including repeated-call query-only requests, marker privacy/corruption recovery, model/content invalidation, and unchanged daemon/protocol/query failure policy in real non-git trackers. Complete PR self-review checked every content-age writer and shared recall/consolidation cache path; no other valid instance or outside-diff finding remains. npm ci succeeded; npm run typecheck and npm run lint passed. Normal-home health flags only an external extension version mismatch; isolated health and full gates follow. No new pm CLI/SDK defect established."
  "2026-10-22T11:20:34.848Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm regression execution passed 4/4 (one linked command, exit 0; persistence disabled by existing project policy). Isolated pm health reports ok=true with no history drift or pending merge receipts. The first npm release run stopped at zero-duplication enforcement because two new assertions repeated a token sequence; rewrote the assertions without changing behaviour or thresholds, then restarted the full gate. No timeout has occurred."
  "2026-10-22T11:35:53.136Z",codex-agent,"Local full npm release checks passed identity, typecheck, lint, zero duplication across 52 measured sources, build and 98 documented declarations in 22 files. The coverage run encountered existing privacy wall-clock failures under severe host contention; an isolated three-case retry also missed the unchanged process or 500ms limits. The new four-case regression command passed via pm, and both independent reverts failed as recorded. Do not weaken deadlines or thresholds. Push the reviewed candidate and require exact-head CI to pass all npm components on Node 22/26 plus the complete Bun release gate before proceeding to PR #6. Strict isolated health passes with required merge drivers and no history drift; normal-home health has an unrelated global extension mismatch. No committed dist files exist."
  "2026-10-22T11:42:00.042Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head Node 22 CI exposed a compatibility mistake in the first pin fix: 202/203 tests passed, but the existing imported-memory regression requires pin changes to reset verification and mark the record edited. The review finding requires preserving content age only. Narrowed remember so content equality controls changed_at, while content OR pin changes retain the existing verification reset and edited marker. Updated the new pin regression and architecture text accordingly; this supersedes earlier comments claiming verification preservation on pin changes. Rejection-cache regressions passed in CI. No deadlines, thresholds, dependency pins or existing tests were weakened. Recheck both the new pin-order regression and the existing imported-memory regression, then rerun exact-head CI."
